{"type":"thinking","text":"Good. My iteration record will include status, newInfoRatio, focus, answeredQuestions, ruledOut, iteration, runId/sessionId/lineageId, timestamp.\n\nNow: the important question of what session/generation is used. step_create_config: lineage.sessionId = session_id_init (the dispatch session id), generation 1. So the lineage config gets fanout-deepseek-1-1794603759690-pm09h3.\n\nLet me now check the reduce-state.cjs invocation requirements: `node reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} [--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}]`. The prompt's exact command: `node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs specs/.../006-purpose-retention-across-handovers --artifact-dir specs/.../006-purpose-retention-across-handovers/research/lineages/deepseek-1`.\n\nNow let me plan the research. This is the substance. The task: answer five numbered questions. Five iterations available.\n\nAlso I should check steer.md existence (does not exist currently). I'll check before each iteration.\n\nLet me plan iterations:\n- Iter 1: Q1 — Where are a packet's problem, purpose and user need written today, per level and for a phase parent, and which of those places is required and validated? Read templates: spec.md.tmpl, phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl, handover.md.tmpl, goal.md.tmpl, acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl; validation rules (required files, level requirements); folder-structure.md §3.\n- Iter 2: Q2 — hop surfaces: Claude compaction hooks (compact-inject.ts, session-prime.ts), other runtimes' hooks under runtime/hooks/, /speckit:resume, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:save + generate-context.js, deep-loop iteration prompts and child-dispatch briefs. Trace what each reads/emits.\n- Iter 3: Q3 — empirical sample of real packets under specs/ with handover.md / continuity saves; measure purpose restatement; phase children drift. Use grep/rg data.\n- Iter 4: Q4 — candidate changes: test operator candidates (parent-level acceptance criteria; parent purpose/user-story section; improved parent-specific spec template) plus alternatives (purpose field in continuity block, compaction brief). Evaluate cost/coverage against evidence; identify lowest-cost closure. Might use implementation files (generate-context.js, validator) to estimate cost.\n- Iter 5: Q5 — what is ruled out and why; consolidate; final iteration before synthesis. Actually Q5 is largely synthesis of earlier iterations' ruled-out. Still, run a fifth iteration with a distinct angle to avoid convergence early: e.g., inspect the resume path's actual field list and the continuity schema (handover/resume docs), plus validate the \"smallest change\" against the validator's required-field rules — i.e., feasibility & cost evidence: which template/validator lines would change, and what a purpose-retention check would cost. That's genuinely new evidence for Q4/Q5.\n\nmaxIterations 5, minIterations 3. Since stopPolicy is max-iterations, I run all 5 regardless of convergence; convergence is telemetry only. The terminal synthesis record stopReason \"maxIterationsReached\".\n\nNow, let me be efficient with tool calls but be thorough — the per-iteration budget in config is maxToolCallsPerIteration 24, and prompt-pack says max {max_tool_calls_per_iteration}. The persona says max 12 per iteration. I'll aim ~10-14 per iteration including writes. Hmm, the agent persona says max 12; config says 24. I'll aim for ≤14 per iteration but prioritize content quality. Actually the YAML agent_config says tool_call_budget target 12, max 24. The prompt pack substitutes max_tool_calls_per_iteration from config = 24. So max is 24. Good — I can batch reads.\n\nFirst, phase_init. Let me do it now carefully:\n\n1. mkdir -p {artifact_dir}/prompts {artifact_dir}/iterations {artifact_dir}/deltas\n2. Create lineage config at {artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json from template, populated. But wait — the packet-level config exists at research/deep-research-config.json. state_paths.config = {artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json. I need the lineage config in lineage dir. I must not modify the packet one.\n\nNote: The containment baseline includes 006.../research/deep-research-config.json — the baseline snapshot taken before my run. Since I only write in the lineage dir, fine.\n\n3. step_create_state_log: gateway run_initialized event.\n4. step_create_strategy: create {artifact_dir}/deep-research-strategy.md with key questions derived (the five questions verbatim, since answeredQuestions must match \"- [ ]\" text exactly).\n5. step_create_registry: {artifact_dir}/findings-registry.json.\n6. Reduce state after each iteration.\n\nNote step_validate_convergence_config: config has minIterations? The packet config has antiConvergence.minIterations: 3. The workflow reads \"minIterations\" from deep-research-config.json — top-level? It says \"Extract numeric minIterations from deep-research-config.json when present\". The packet config has minIterations only under antiConvergence. Since stopPolicy is max-iterations, it doesn't matter much. I'll include minIterations: 3 top-level in lineage config to be safe.\n\nLet me check the config template to produce a correct lineage config.\n\nAlso: does reduce-state.cjs need a config at the artifact dir? Let me check its arg parsing and what files it expects. Let me grep the head of reduce-state.cjs."}
