{"type":"tool_result","callId":"call_596c2b9ca29a41048acc5013","status":"completed","result":"\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The rotate-logs script never deletes old archives, so a host that copies `logs/archive` fills its disk. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\n\n### Purpose\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: One-sentence outcome statement. What does success look like?]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n<!-- FILL: Run the command this change affects and paste the command and its verbatim output. Quote every number the spec states about current behavior from this block. Write `N/A:` and a reason when no command applies. GOOD: `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh` with 10 archives, then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: The script deletes old logs. -->\n```text\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: command and its verbatim output]\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. Before you list a new file, module, option, layer or dependency, name what fails today without it, or drop it. GOOD: Add a `--keep <n>` option that deletes all but the newest n archives in `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->\n\n### In Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 2]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 3]\n\n### Out of Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 1] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 2] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path/to/file.js] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Modify/Create/Delete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Write one testable requirement per row. Name the exact command or output. GOOD: With 10 archives, `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh --keep 3` exits 0 and `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3. WEAK: The option should work well. -->\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n<!-- IF level:1 -->\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to verify it's done] |\n<!-- /IF -->\n<!-- IF level:2,3,3+ -->\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] |\n<!-- /IF -->\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n<!-- IF level:1 -->\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-002 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to verify it's done] |\n<!-- /IF -->\n<!-- IF level:2,3,3+ -->\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-002 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /IF -->\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: With 10 archives in `logs/archive`, `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh --keep 3` leaves 3. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n===== PHASE PARENT =====\n# Feature Specification: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: feature-name]\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 2 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | [YYYY-MM-DD] |\n| **Branch** | `main` |\n| **Parent Spec** | `../spec.md` |\n| **Parent Packet** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: packet-id] |\n| **Predecessor** | [Predecessor-packet] |\n| **Successor** | [Successor-packet, or \"None\"] |\n| **Handoff Criteria** | Validator + template + generator changes ship so parent validates under tolerant policy |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n[One-paragraph problem statement — what needs solving and why]\n\n### Purpose\n[One-paragraph purpose — what this phased decomposition achieves]\n\n> **Phase-parent note:** This spec.md is the ONLY authored document at the parent level. All detailed planning, task breakdowns, checklists, and decisions live in the child phase folders listed in the Phase Documentation Map below. This keeps the parent from drifting stale as phases execute and pivot.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n[Bullet list of what this phase decomposition covers]\n\n### Out of Scope\n[Bullet list of what is explicitly excluded]\n\n### Files to Change\n[Summary table of files touched across all phases — for audit trail only; per-phase detail lives in each child's plan.md]\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Phase | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------|-------------|\n| [Path] | [Modify/Create] | [Phase-name] | [Description] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n## PHASE DOCUMENTATION MAP\n\n> This spec uses phased decomposition. Each phase is an independently executable child spec folder. All implementation details (plan, tasks, checklist, decisions, continuity) live inside the phase children.\n\n| Phase | Folder | Focus | Status |\n|-------|--------|-------|--------|\n<!-- [PHASE_ROW] — Replaced by create.sh with full 4-column table rows -->\n\n### Phase Transition Rules\n\n- Each phase MUST pass `validate.sh` independently before the next phase begins\n- Parent spec tracks aggregate progress via this map\n- Use `/speckit:resume [parent-folder]/[NNN-phase]/` to resume a specific phase\n- Run `validate.sh --recursive` on parent to validate all phases as integrated unit\n\n### Phase Handoff Criteria\n\n| From | To | Criteria | Verification |\n|------|-----|----------|--------------|\n<!-- [HANDOFF_ROW] — Replaced by create.sh with full 4-column table rows -->\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 4. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- [Open question 1]\n- [Open question 2]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Phase children**: See sub-folders `[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/` for per-phase spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md\n- **Parent Spec**: See `../spec.md`\n- **Graph Metadata**: See `graph-metadata.json` for `derived.last_active_child_id` pointer\n<!-- /IF -->\n"}
