{"type":"thinking","text":"Important: \n- ANCHORS_VALID does NOT diff against template anchors for presence of specific section anchors — it only checks well-formedness of whatever anchors exist. And it exempts phase parents entirely: \"A phase parent carries a lean document set by design and has always been exempt here\" [SOURCE: orchestrator.ts:966-975].\n- Level contract: requiredCoreDocs for level 1 = ['spec.md','plan.md','tasks.md'] per tests.\n\nLet me read the level contract resolver source to state precisely what files are required per level and where handover/goal/acceptance-criteria sit (lazyAddonDocs vs optionalAddonDocs). Find the source file.\n\nAlso I want to check what `seed_reference_documents` is invoked under — conditional? Let me look at function name near line 640 and its call site.\n\nLet me be efficient: I have enough for Q1 core. I need:\n(a) level contract file (exact lists).\n(b) whether handover.md scaffolded by default (create.sh call site).\n(c) validation rule list default (which rules run) — from validate.sh or rules registry.\n(d) resume/handoff/save surfaces for iteration 2.\n\nLet me grab (a) and (b) now, then write iteration 1.\n\nActually, for Q1 the \"user need\" part: is there any place recording \"user need\"? spec.md has PROBLEM & PURPOSE; goal.md has Objective + Decisions + COMPLETION CRITERIA; acceptance-criteria has none; handover has none. Also implementation-summary has `_memory.continuity` block (per spec.md) with fields listed. Let me check implementation-summary template for the continuity block (this is central: the continuity block is the compaction surface, no purpose field).\n\nLet me batch: level-contract resolver source, create.sh call site of seed function, implementation-summary.md.tmpl continuity fields."}
