{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-b44d7839011bb788","status":"completed","result":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:52:## 2. RULE SUMMARY\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:56:| `FILE_EXISTS`        | ERROR    | All levels    | Required files present for documentation level |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:57:| `PLACEHOLDER_FILLED` | ERROR or WARNING | Core files | No unfilled template tokens. A v2.3 doc warns while Draft |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:58:| `LEVEL_DECLARED`     | INFO     | spec.md       | Level explicitly stated in metadata            |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:59:| `AC_COVERAGE`        | INFO     | acceptance-criteria.md | Advisory traceability scan over each criterion's Verification cell (on by default; `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE=true` makes an under-floor result fail) |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:60:| `AC_CLOSURE`         | ERROR    | acceptance-criteria.md | Closure gate for Levels 2/3/3+: unmet criteria block a completion claim, waivers must cite a real ADR |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:61:| `CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS` | WARNING | completion claims | Opt-in strict-only completion freshness check |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:62:| `ANCHORS_VALID`      | ERROR    | spec docs with anchored templates | Anchors present, paired and not nested (adr-NNN may hold adr-NNN-*); a v2.3 doc also keeps each anchor its template requires |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:63:| `FOLDER_NAMING`      | ERROR    | Folder path   | Folder follows ###-short-name convention       |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:64:| `FRONTMATTER_VALID`  | ERROR    | spec docs     | YAML frontmatter properly structured           |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:65:| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:66:| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:67:| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:68:| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:69:| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:70:| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:71:| `MEASURED_BEHAVIOR` | WARNING  | spec.md stamped v2.4+ | `measured-behavior` anchor present with the changed command's verbatim output, or an `N/A:` line with a reason |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:176:| `SPECKIT_AC_TRACEABILITY_TEMPLATE` | `false` | Reserved opt-in for future scaffold template rendering of traceability rows. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:177:| `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE` | `true` | Runs the advisory validation scan by default; set to `false` to opt out. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:178:| `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE` | `false` | `true` fails an under-floor result for a packet created after the coverage cutoff. An older packet stays advisory, and the default keeps every packet advisory. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:179:| `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_FLOOR` | `0.9` | Sets the advisory coverage floor, clamped to `[0,1]`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:201:| `SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS` | `false` | Enables strict-only completion freshness validation. When on, a stale result reports a warning, which does not block. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:202:| `SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE` | `false` | Escalates a stale-freshness `warn` to an `error`, which makes `--strict` exit 2. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:864:| `SPECKIT_VALIDATION` | true    | Set to `false` to skip validation |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:865:| `SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION` | unset | Set to `1`, `true`, `yes` or `on` to skip validation, in the environment or saved in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`. The environment wins over the file. A skipped run exits 0 and under `--json` prints a report marked `skipped: true` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:866:| `SPECKIT_STRICT`     | false   | Set to `true` to run the strict-only rules |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:867:| `SPECKIT_JSON`       | false   | Set to `true` for JSON output     |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:868:| `SPECKIT_VERBOSE`    | false   | Set to `true` for verbose output  |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:869:| `SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE` | unset | Set to `1` during scaffolding to run `validate.sh --quiet` after `create.sh` writes files |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:877:It runs only when `spec.md` Status is Draft and every error is a derived-metadata one. It never runs for any other status, when any content rule fails, without `--strict`, when `SPECKIT_RULES` names a subset of rules, or when `CI` is set: a check in CI reads a committed tree and must not rewrite it. The last three keep \"every error is derived\" honest, since a narrowed or non-strict run never ran some content rules. `SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=0` turns it off, as do `false` and `off`. Tools that run `validate.sh` as a child to read or audit a packet set the switch to `0`, so only a person or model running the validator directly gets the repair. A recursive run, including the one `validate.sh` starts by itself on a phase parent, validates each child as its own packet, so every Draft child whose errors are all derived gets its own repair, and each rewrite is printed. Set the switch to `0` to check a phase parent without writing. `validateFolder` called as a library never writes.\n"}
