{"type":"thinking","text":"Key facts for Q1:\n- User stories section only at Level 3/3+ (inside `<!-- IF level:3,3+ -->`) — so user need (as \"As a X I want Y so that Z\") is written only at Level 3+; Level 1/2 have no user-need section at all. That's a strong finding: the \"user need\" has no home at Level 1/2 except prose in Problem Statement.\n- TOKEN_GATE_MIN_MAJOR/MINOR: need the value. Let me check constants quickly... I'll infer: template stamp v2.4 tokens; the gate at v2.3 means v2.4 docs PASS carriesTokenGateStamp (>2.3) and thus ARE checked for required anchors! Wait: `major > TOKEN_GATE_MIN_MAJOR || (major === MIN && minor >= MIN_MINOR)`. If TOKEN_GATE_MIN = 2.3, then v2.4 → 2>2 false, 2==2 && 4>=3 true → true. So v2.4 docs DO carry the token gate stamp, and are checked for required anchors. Hmm. That means the comment \"A v2.3 doc must keep every section its template requires... Older docs keep the integrity-only check\" means v2.3+ docs are checked, older ones aren't. So v2.4 spec.md requires all sections whose H2 headers are not L2:/L3: prefixed — including \"## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\" (anchor `problem`).\n\nWait, but requiredTemplateSections only includes anchors where an H2 header inside the anchor is \"required\" (not prefixed by L2:/L3:/FIX ADDENDUM). The `problem` anchor contains \"## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\" (required) → included. So deleting the whole PROBLEM & PURPOSE section fails ANCHORS_VALID in v2.4 docs. But leaving the heading in place with empty/placeholder text: anchor body non-empty check passes if placeholder retained; PLACEHOLDER_FILLED catches `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:` tokens.\n\nCrucially, what does NOT happen: no rule checks that Problem Statement *content* actually states a problem, and the phase parent is explicitly exempt from ANCHORS_VALID entirely (\"Phase parent lean document set accepted\" [SOURCE: orchestrator.ts:966-970]). But SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY applies to phase parents (collectDocuments uses level contract; level 'phase' gates key 'purpose' — but SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY's missing-anchor check only applies to timeline/goal). So for a phase parent, spec.md may omit the problem/purpose section entirely and validation passes.\n\nWait — is that true? For phase level, validationDocsForLevel might be lean (spec.md only). ANCHORS_VALID short-circuits: `if (level === 'phase' && isPhaseParent(folder)) return pass`. So yes.\n\nLet me verify TOKEN_GATE_MIN constants to be exact.\n\nAlso PLACEHOLDER_FILLED: check whether a Draft status downgrades to warning, and whether `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE` in spec.md counts. Yes PLACEHOLDER_MARKER_RE includes `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:`. But what about a fully-filled spec vs empty section? If author deletes placeholder text but leaves heading empty, anchor empty → SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY error \"is empty\". OK.\n\nOne more: phase-parent template has same problem/purpose but the phase-parent.spec template's PROBLEM & PURPOSE is a required H2? It's under `<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->`. So even at phase level, if ANCHORS_VALID weren't exempted, it would be required.\n\nLet me now check TOKEN_GATE constants and then write iteration 1. Also worth capturing: acceptance-criteria template has no user/purpose column (CRITERIA table). Let me quickly read its CRITERIA section for column definitions (for Q4 candidate cost)."}
