{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-b8fa9eba739064e4","status":"completed","result":"758:const TOKEN_GATE_MIN_MAJOR = 2;\n759:const TOKEN_GATE_MIN_MINOR = 3;\n760:const TEMPLATE_STAMP_RE = /^\\s*<!--\\s*SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE:[^|>]*\\|\\s*v(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)\\s*-->/u;\n764:    const stamp = TEMPLATE_STAMP_RE.exec(line);\n768:    return major > TOKEN_GATE_MIN_MAJOR || (major === TOKEN_GATE_MIN_MAJOR && minor >= TOKEN_GATE_MIN_MINOR);\n=== AC TEMPLATE CRITERIA ===\n## 2. CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one row per requirement. The Then clause names a command. GOOD: AC-001: When `--keep 3` runs, Then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3. WEAK: The feature works. -->\n\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: context], When [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: action], Then [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: observable outcome] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: command, file:line, or artifact that proves it] | Unmet | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n\nWrite `-` when the row is `Met` or `Unmet`. Write `ADR-NNN` when the row is\n`Waived` or `Superseded`, naming a decision record that exists in\n`decision-record.md`. A waiver naming an ADR that is not there fails validation:\nthe point of a waiver is that someone recorded the reasoning, so an unbacked\nwaiver is treated as an unmet criterion rather than as a pass.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:closure -->\n## 3. CLOSURE STATEMENT\n<!-- FILL: Write Yes or No and one sentence. Name a criterion by its id only when it blocks closure. Never write a count of criteria or an id range, because every added row makes it wrong. GOOD: No. AC-002 is unmet. WEAK: All eight criteria AC-001 to AC-008 are met. -->\n\n**Closeable:** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n\n[One sentence: what decides closure now. Name a criterion by id only when it blocks closure.]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:closure -->\n<!-- /IF -->\n"}
