{"type":"thinking","text":"Good. Now I have plenty for Q1. Let me write iteration 1.\n\nFindings for iteration 1 (Q1):\n1. Every level's spec template writes the problem/purpose once, in `## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE` with Problem Statement + Purpose [SOURCE: templates/core/spec.md.tmpl:99-107]. Phase parent has the same section [SOURCE: templates/packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl:63-72].\n2. User need has no dedicated authored field at Levels 1-2: the only \"As a… I want… so that…\" section is `## 11. USER STORIES`, emitted only for level:3,3+ [SOURCE: templates/core/spec.md.tmpl:326,340-347]. Level 1/2 packets therefore carry user need only as prose inside Problem Statement.\n3. Level contract: required core docs are spec.md/plan.md/tasks.md for L1-3; implementation-summary.md only after implementation starts; handover.md and goal.md are `lazyAddonDocs` (scaffolded on request); acceptance-criteria.md is optional addon at L2/3 (required via AC_CLOSURE rule for packets after 2026-08-30) [SOURCE: templates/spec-kit-docs.json levels..., folder-structure.md:158-190]. The phase level requires only spec.md [manifest phase row].\n4. Required-and-validated: the `problem` anchor is required for spec.md at levels 1,2,3,3+ through the section-gate table [spec-kit-docs.json sectionGates[\"spec.md\"].problem]. Enforcement is via ANCHORS_VALID's v2.3+ token gate: docs stamped v2.3+ must keep every required template anchor [orchestrator.ts:758-768, 1028-1035]. So a v2.4 spec.md that deletes the PROBLEM & PURPOSE section fails ANCHORS_VALID.\n5. BUT: the phase parent is explicitly exempt from ANCHORS_VALID [orchestrator.ts:966-970 \"Phase parent lean document set accepted\"], and SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY's missing-anchor loop only covers timeline.md/goal.md [spec-doc-structure.ts:1182-1191]. So a phase parent's spec.md can lose Problem & Purpose entirely and still validate. This is the validated-gap at parent level.\n6. No validation rule reads the words content-wise: grep count 0 for