{"type":"thinking","text":"Important detail: the phase level's spec.md gates DO include `problem` [\"phase\"] — so the manifest requires `problem` for phase-parent spec.md. But ANCHORS_VALID has the explicit phase-parent exemption (orchestrator.ts:966-970), and SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY only enforces missing anchors for timeline/goal. So the manifest gate `problem` for phase is declared but not enforced for phase parents because the only enforcement path (ANCHORS_VALID's requiredTemplateSections loop) is short-circuited by the exemption for phase parents. That's an important nuance — the *declared* contract says required, the *executed* check exempts.\n\nLet me confirm that requiredTemplateSections at level 'phase' would include `problem` if it weren't exempted — yes because renderedTemplate(level='phase', docName='spec.md') = phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl, whose H2 \"## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\" is required (no L2:/L3: prefix) and anchor `problem` wraps it.\n\nThis is a strong, precise answer to Q1.\n\nNow write iteration 1. Files:\n- iterations/iteration-001.md\n- deltas/iter-001.jsonl (iteration row + finding rows + maybe ruled_out)\n- gateway record file (one JSON object) then gateway call\n- then reduce-state\n\nnewInfoRatio = 1.0 (all new). findingsCount = 9.\n\nIteration record fields:\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"runId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1-1794603759690-pm09h3\",\"sessionId\":\"...\",\"lineageId\":\"...\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Q1 — where problem/purpose/user need are written per level and phase parent, and which of those places are required and validated\",\"findingsCount\":9,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All nine findings are new: this is the first measurement of the purpose-bearing template sections and their enforcement paths in the validator.\",\"keyQuestions\":[...5...],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Where are a packet's problem, purpose and user need written today, per level and for a phase parent, and which of those places is required and validated?\"],\"ruledOut\":[],\"focusTrack\":\"purpose-surfaces\",\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\",\"Glob\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[...],\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"durationMs\":N,\"graphEvents\":[...]}\n\nShould I mark Q1 answered? Yes — I have enough cited evidence to answer it. The reducer ticks the box only on exact text match. The strategy text is exact. Good.\n\ngraphEvents: optional — I'll include a few QUESTION/FINDING/SOURCE nodes and edges to feed the coverage graph. That helps graph convergence telemetry. Keep shapes exact. The prompt-pack says graph nodes with SOURCE kind naming a file MUST carry \"path\". Actually: \"every SOURCE graph node that names a file MUST carry \"path\"\". I'll include path fields.\n\nLet me compute durationMs: start ~21:03:42 (gateway), now maybe 21:10. I'll compute from init time roughly. Not critical; I'll put a plausible elapsed value computed from `date`.\n\nLet me write iteration 1 narrative now. Use headings per contract: Focus, Actions Taken, Findings, Questions Answered, Questions Remaining, Next Focus — plus the persona's required sections (Ruled Out, Dead Ends, Edge Cases, Sources Consulted, Assessment, Reflection, Recommended Next Focus). I'll include both sets, ensuring the pack's required headings exist.\n\nThen delta: iteration row + 9 finding rows with sources arrays + 1 ruled_out maybe none.\n\nThen gateway.\n\nLet me write."}
