{"type":"thinking","text":"MAJOR finding for Q2: The continuity facets labeled \"Goal\" are populated from `next_safe_action` — not from any purpose. So the compaction injection's \"Goal\" facet is actually the next action. This is the exact mechanism by which the post-compaction context shows only mechanics: \"Goal\" = next_safe_action, \"Decision\" = answered questions, \"Progress\" = recent action + touched files, \"Gotcha\" = blockers + open questions.\n\nThat's a crisp answer to why the observed compaction stated files/counts/topics with no purpose.\n\nNow, does compact-inject include spec.md content? It has `detectSpecFolder` and `buildMergedCompactResult` which uses transcript analysis (file paths, topics, attention signals) — i.e., derived from the transcript, not from spec docs. The authored snapshot path is optional (`authoredSnapshotEnabled` requires input flag authored_continuity_snapshot===true or continuity_snapshot==='authored'). Let me confirm: `function authoredSnapshotEnabled(input)` returns flag; and `runAuthoredSnapshot` probably only when enabled. So by default the PreCompact hook builds context from transcript lines (topics, file paths) — no spec-doc read at all.\n\nLet me verify: in buildMergedCompactResult (line 443-530), does it read spec.md? Let me read 440-535 quickly. And check session-prime.ts: what it injects at session start (probably \"packet pointer + continuity block + next safe action\").\n\nLet me read both chunks."}
