{"type":"thinking","text":"Confirmed: the default PreCompact path builds context from the transcript tail only: active files, recent topics, attention signals, recent context, plus detected spec folder. It never reads spec.md or the packet docs. The authored-snapshot path is opt-in by flag.\n\nSession-prime: on startup it emits a static fallback surface: \"Continuity: recover on demand from the packet docs\", plus \"/speckit:resume — recover the active packet from its canonical docs\" and \"rg over specs/\". So the session-prime hook points at recovery but carries no purpose itself. On compact, it says \"Context was compacted. Run /speckit:resume ...\". So session start provides pointers, not content.\n\nNow `/speckit:resume`: the resume ladder reads handover.md (highest), then _memory.continuity, then spec docs; priority list includes implementation-summary, spec.md, plan.md... The ladder likely extracts a bounded excerpt. Need: does the ladder include spec.md's problem/purpose? It reads spec.md as a spec-doc but likely only extracts specific signals (hints? \"ResumeSignal\"). Let me read the ladder's spec-doc extraction (maybe `extractSignals` reads \"Next Safe Action\", \"Blockers\" from specs, not purpose). Also the resume restore panel: RESTORE_PANEL_MAX_ITEMS 8, MAX_CHARS 1200 — so only a bounded set of items; from `buildRestorePanel`.\n\nLet me read the resume-ladder relevant parts: around 600-700 (handover snapshot) and buildRestorePanel 507-560, and the spec-doc signal extraction (search \"function .*Signal\" / \"extract\"). Also read `/speckit:resume` command doc for stated contract.\n\nLet me batch: grep for function names in resume-ladder and read 880-1080 region maybe. Let me first list functions."}
