{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-88d6a3e90da5d19a","status":"completed","result":"\n## 3. Results Display\n\n### Resume Brief\n\n```text\nRESUME BRIEF\nSpec: [path]\nConfidence: [high|medium|low] | Source: [handover|continuity|spec_docs|mcp_enrichment|combined]\nNow: [phase/current task]\nLast confirmed: [action]\nNext safe action: [action]\nBlockers: [none|details]\nProgress: [X]% ([done]/[total] tasks)\nWhy this is next: [short reason based on tasks/checklist/memory]\n```\n\n### No Session\n\n```text\nNo active SpecKit session found.\nProvide a spec folder path or start a new packet with /speckit:complete.\nSTATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"no active session\"\n```\n\n### Next-Step Suggestions\n=== HANDOFF CMD ===\n42:- When a spec packet is bound: save continuity before `prepare` runs. The nudge asks for the note first, and either order works. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to the continuity writer.\n61:| 2 | Save the packet | Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes use the continuity writer when a packet is bound | Fresh continuity |\n78:When `spec_folder` is a packet path, save its continuity before `prepare` so the receiving session's `/speckit:resume` lands on fresh state.\n83:Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --stdin --full-auto <spec-folder>`.\n88:If the save fails, stop here. Do not write the note or run `prepare`, because the receiving session would resume stale packet state. Report `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"continuity save failed: <reason>\"`.\n235:- `/speckit:save`: used before the note on Claude when a spec packet is bound. Other runtimes use the continuity writer.\n[exit code: 1]"}
