{"type":"thinking","text":"Handoff: \"save continuity before prepare\"; the handover note template has no purpose section (already confirmed). Resume brief fields: Spec, Confidence, Source, Now, Last confirmed, Next safe action, Blockers, Progress, Why this is next — no Purpose/Goal.\n\nI now have a thorough Q2 answer. Let me write iteration 2.\n\nFindings for Q2 (each surface, read/emit, does purpose travel):\n\n1. Claude PreCompact (`compact-inject.ts`) reads only the live transcript tail and writes a merged brief from four selectors — active files, recent topics, working-memory attention signals, recent context — plus a detected \"Active spec folder\" path. It never opens spec.md, handover.md or the continuity block [SOURCE: compact-inject.ts:443-492, 459-484]. Purpose does not travel; the packet is represented by a path string.\n2. The authored continuity snapshot path exists but is opt-in: `authoredSnapshotEnabled(input)` requires the input to set `authored_continuity_snapshot: true` or `continuity_snapshot: 'authored'` [SOURCE: compact-inject.ts:348-355, 608-630]. Default compaction does not run it.\n3. Even when it runs, the injected facets carry no purpose: `buildContinuityFacets` fills the \"Goal\" facet from `next_safe_action`, \"Decision\" from answered-question ids, \"Progress\" from recent_action + summary + touched files, \"Gotcha\" from blockers + open questions [SOURCE: thin-continuity-record.ts:289-303, 307-323]. The label \"Goal\" is the next action, not the packet's objective — a direct mechanism for the operator's observed \"mechanics but no purpose\".\n4. Claude's session-prime hook emits no packet content at startup: fallback surface is \"CONTINUITY: recover on demand from the packet docs\" plus pointers to /speckit:resume and rg over specs/; on compact it prints \"Context was compacted. Run /speckit:resume ...\" [SOURCE: session-prime.ts:230-258, 135-170]. So startup carries pointers, not purpose.\n5. Codex's PreCompact adapter delegates to the Claude compact-inject build (`runClaudeHookAdapter('compact-inject.js', ...)`) [SOURCE: hooks/codex/compact-inject.ts:36-38], and dsh/cursor equivalents import the same shared payload; pi and devin do have compact handlers but their \"rehydrate\" step only writes \"## Active Spec Folder\\n<path>\" plus the recovery pointer [SOURCE: hooks/pi/session-compact-context.ts:141-190; hooks/devin/post-compaction.cjs:270-290]. No runtime's compaction hook re-reads spec.md's problem or purpose.\n6. `/speckit:resume`'s ladder parses three tiers into a fixed signal shape — summary, recentAction, nextSafeAction, blockers, keyFiles, documents [+packetPointer] — with no purpose/problem/objective field [SOURCE: resume-ladder.ts:56-72; 632-712; 758-790]. The handover tier reads only labeled values `Recent action`, `Next safe action`, `Blockers`, `Key files` [632-640]; the spec-docs tier synthesizes \"Review tasks.md and continue the packet.\" as the next action and takes only title + first three non-heading lines as summary [758-790].\n7. The resume brief shown to the operator has fields Spec / Confidence / Source / Now / Last confirmed / Next safe action / Blockers / Progress / Why this is next, with no purpose line [SOURCE: commands/speckit/assets/speckit-resume-presentation.txt:116-129]. The restore panel is capped at 8 items and 1,200 chars [resume-ladder.ts:149-150, 507-560], so even a purpose string would compete with next-action items.\n8. `/speckit:handoff` saves continuity then writes a handover note; the handover template has no purpose heading and the resume parser would not read one even if written (it extracts only Recent action / Next safe action / Blockers / Key files; a purpose paragraph could appear only if it fell into the first three plain lines via collectSummaryLines) [SOURCE: commands/speckit/handoff.md:42,61,78-88; handover.md.tmpl:37-121; resume-ladder.ts:632-640, 405-417].\n9. `/speckit:save` + generate-context writes a compact continuity record whose documented payload fields are recent_action, next_safe_action, blockers, key_files (plus completion_pct, open/answered questions); no purpose field exists in the contract [SOURCE: generate-context.ts:170-181; thin-continuity-record.ts:60-78]. A purpose can only survive the save if a later reader treats spec.md as a document, not via the continuity block.\n10. The one hop that does carry purpose-shaped text is the deep-loop child brief: fanout-run's `buildLoopPrompt` injects `research_topic: <full topic>` into the child prompt [SOURCE: fanout-run.cjs:1655-1669, 1547-1560], and the iteration prompt pack renders `{research_topic}` plus focus/questions for every iteration [SOURCE: prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:11-16]. So research loops restate purpose by construction; ordinary implementation sessions have no equivalent field.\n\nThat's 10 findings. newInfoRatio: all new → 1.0. Q2 answered.\n\nWait — one caution: \"dsh/cursor equivalents import the same shared payload\" — I haven't verified that. I should not claim without evidence. Let me soften: I verified codex delegates to claude's adapter; pi/devin compose their own with no continuity facets. I should quickly check dsh and cursor to make the claim complete. dsh/session-compact-context.mjs grep showed no continuity mentions. Let me look at it briefly (30 lines) to characterize. And cursor/precompact.ts. That's 2 quick greps — worth it for accuracy.\n\nLet me do that, then write."}
