{"type":"thinking","text":"Confirmed: dsh runs the shared claude session-prime hook (SESSION_PRIME_PATH) and uses its output as compaction base context. So the dsh compaction path = claude session-prime output (pointers) + recovery pointer.\n\nNow write iteration 2. Findings (10). Let me be precise with citations and line numbers I actually saw:\n\n- compact-inject.ts:443-492 (buildMergedCompactResult; topic/file selectors), :459-484 (sessionParts), :348-355 (authoredSnapshotEnabled), :608-630 (runAuthoredSnapshot worker).\n- thin-continuity-record.ts:289-303 (buildContinuityFacets mapping), :307-323 (labels Goal/Decision/Progress/Gotcha). Careful: grep output showed buildContinuityFacets at some line; the sed showed it after 289. I know fields at 60-78. I'll cite :289-303 and :307-323 approximately. Risky if wrong. Let me verify exact line numbers of buildContinuityFacets. Quick grep -n.\n\nAlso resume-ladder line numbers: 56-72 (interface), 149-150 constants (RESTORE_PANEL_MAX_ITEMS at 149? earlier buildRestorePanel at 507, MAX_ITEMS constant around 149-150), 405-417 collectSummaryLines, 632-712 parseHandoverSignal/parseContinuitySignal, 758-790 parseSpecDocumentSignal. From grep: RESTORE_PANEL_MAX_ITEMS = 8 is right after SPEC_DOC_PRIORITY (152-162?). The output showed constants after interface at 133-142: `keyFiles`, `documents`, `packetPointer`, then constants starting 146; FRONTMATTER_RE, SPEC_DOC_PRIORITY (9 entries), RESTORE_PANEL_MAX_ITEMS, RESTORE_PANEL_MAX_CHARS, PHASE_PARENT_REDIRECT_MAX_DEPTH, PHASE_CHILD_NAME_RE. So RESTORE_PANEL_MAX_ITEMS ≈ 152, MAX_CHARS ≈ 153. I'll cite :146-153 instead of 149-150 to be safe? Better: cite the function buildRestorePanel at :507-560 which I read, and mention caps there. The caps are read at line ~528-535 inside. I'll cite :507-560.\n\nAlso session-prime.ts:230-258 (buildFallbackStartupSurface+handleStartup), :135-170 (handleCompact). From grep: handleCompact at 135, buildFallbackStartupSurface at 230, handleStartup at 241. Good.\n\ndsh: session-compact-context.mjs:7 (import runSessionPrime), :122 (recovery pointer), :126-142 (compose). session-start-context.mjs:44-58 (runSessionPrime spawns SESSION_PRIME_PATH).\n\ndevin/post-compaction.cjs:270-290 (composeRecoverySections steps 1-3), :266 (recovery pointer).\npi/session-compact-context.ts:141-190.\ncursor/precompact.ts:28-35,60 (delegates to claude adapter). Hmm — line 60 is runCursorHook(import.meta.url, main); line 28-33 imports from shared. I didn't confirm it runs claude adapter. It imports notifyDirectiveLifecycleBoundary and readCursorHookInput? Not certain. Let me avoid claiming cursor delegates; instead say cursor's precompact.ts is a thin proxy wiring the shared run*Hook helper and imports the claude directive-lifecycle-boundary, with no continuity read of its own (grep for continuity/purpose returned nothing). That's defensible: the grep for continuity|purpose|handover|spec.md returned zero hits in cursor/precompact.ts.\n\nHmm, actually the second grep did include \"continuity|purpose|problem|handover|next_safe|recent_action|spec.md\" for codex only, not cursor. I ran a separate grep for cursor with \"import|continuity|summary|spec|recovery|prompt\" which showed no continuity. So claim: no continuity/purpose handling in the file.\n\nBetter to keep cursor out or state narrowly: \"cursor's precompact proxy contains no continuity or purpose read (grep: zero matches for continuity/purpose/handover/spec.md)\". I can run one grep to be certain. Cheaper: state only verified runtimes (claude, codex, dsh, pi, devin) and note cursor/opencode were not exhaustively traced — that's honest but weakens the answer. One quick grep for all runtimes' compact handlers for \"continuity|purpose|problem\" would settle it. Let me do one grep across hooks dir for \"SPECKIT_CONTINUITY_SNAPSHOT|buildResumeLadder|authored-continuity-snapshot\" to see which runtimes use the snapshot path.\n\nLet me do that single grep + get buildContinuityFacets line number in one call."}
