{"type":"thinking","text":"5523 spec.md, 97 handover.md. That's a big corpus, good for measurement.\n\nMeasurements to make:\n1. Among the 97 packets with handover.md: does the handover restate the purpose? Count handover.md files containing \"purpose|Purpose|problem|Problem|objective|Objective|goal|Goal\" (excluding frontmatter trigger phrases maybe). Better: count headings; and count occurrences of \"PROBLEM & PURPOSE\" in handover (expected 0).\n2. Among packets: how many spec.md have the PROBLEM & PURPOSE section with placeholder text vs filled? Use rg: `\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE` inside the problem anchor? Simpler: count spec.md with \"## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\" heading (older packets may differ), and count those with `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE` anywhere in the file (unfilled). And count spec.md with a \"Purpose\" line whose text is empty/placeholder.\n3. Phase children: measure whether a child's purpose restates the parent's. Approach: for the biggest phase parent (70 children), compare parent problem/purpose text vs child problem/purpose text. Compute overlap? A heuristic: extract the parent's Purpose section text and check how many children contain a Purpose section that is non-placeholder, and how many share distinctive words from the parent's purpose.\n\nThis is qualitative-heavy; I should be careful to report exactly what I measured with commands, and keep claims narrow.\n\nAlso: \"several continuity saves\" — packets with continuity blocks: 4657 implementation-summary.md files. Does the continuity block ever carry a purpose? Measure: grep `-?purpose` or \"purpose\" within _memory.continuity blocks. A quick measure: `rg -l \"purpose:\" specs --glob implementation-summary.md` (frontmatter inside continuity?) and count \"objective:\". Let me measure whether any continuity block has a purpose-like key: `rg -n \"^\\s+(purpose|goal|objective|problem):\" --glob implementation-summary.md specs | wc -l`.\n\nAlso: handover.md content check: `rg -il \"purpose|problem statement|objective\" --glob handover.md specs` count. Then sample 3 to see what they say.\n\nAnd: do phase children restate parent purpose? Take parent `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/001-system-speckit-v4` (70 children) — check parent spec.md Purpose text, then children's purpose texts. Use a script to extract the Purpose section from each spec.md and report: filled vs placeholder, and top shared tokens.\n\nLet me do it in one or two bash calls with a node script. Be careful not to write anywhere except stdout.\n\nLet me write a node script that:\n- walks specs, finds spec.md (exclude research/, _archive/ maybe include? exclude z_archive)\n- extracts section \"## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\" body (up to next ##), and the \"### Purpose\" subsection text.\n- classifies: missing section, placeholder (contains [YOUR_VALUE_HERE or [One-paragraph or [YOUR]), empty, filled.\n- reports totals.\n- phase parents: dirs with ≥2 child dirs; for one parent, show parent purpose text (truncated) and a sample of child purposes with a similarity measure (shared significant words count).\n\nLet me run it."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-812786c9ba098686","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/371-purpose-retention-research && node <<'NODE'\nconst fs=require('fs'), path=require('path');\nfunction walk(dir, out){ let ents; try{ents=fs.readdirSync(dir,{withFileTypes:true});}catch{return out;} for(const e of ents){ if(e.name==='_archive'||e.name==='z_archive'||e.name==='node_modules'||e.name==='.git') continue; const p=path.join(dir,e.name); if(e.isDirectory()) walk(p,out); else if(e.name==='spec.md') out.push(p);} return out;}\nconst files=walk('specs',[]);\nlet missing=0, placeholder=0, filled=0, empty=0;\nconst filledList=[];\nfor(const f of files){\n  const t=fs.readFileSync(f,'utf8');\n  const m=t.match(/<!--\\s*ANCHOR:problem\\s*-->([\\s\\S]*?)<!--\\s*\\/ANCHOR:problem\\s*-->/);\n  if(!m){ missing++; continue; }\n  const body=m[1];\n  const pm=body.match(/###\\s*Purpose\\s*\\n([\\s\\S]*?)(?=\\n#{2,3}\\s|\\n<!--|$)/);\n  const ptext=(pm?pm[1]:'').trim();\n  if(/\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE|\\[One-paragraph|\\[One sentence|\\[YOUR/.test(ptext)) placeholder++;\n  else if(ptext.length===0) empty++;\n  else { filled++; filledList.push([f,ptext.slice(0,120)]); }\n}\nconsole.log('spec.md with problem anchor:', files.length-missing, 'missing anchor:', missing);\nconsole.log('purpose: filled',filled,'placeholder',placeholder,'empty',empty);\nconsole.log('sample filled:'); for(const [f,t] of filledList.slice(0,5)) console.log(' -',f,'::',t.replace(/\\n/g,' '));\nNODE","description":"Measure problem/purpose fill state across 5523 specs"}}
