{"type":"thinking","text":"Interesting: 94 phase parents carry goal.md (lazy addon!) while only 10 carry acceptance-criteria.md. This is strong evidence for the parent-level candidate ranking:\n- The parent-level artifact authors actually create is goal.md (94 parents), not acceptance-criteria.md (10 parents).\n- goal.md already has the durable Objective one-liner; so the purpose *is* available at parent level in 94 packets, yet hops don't read goal.md (iteration 2: no hook imports it; resume ladder SPEC_DOC_PRIORITY has no 'goal.md' — check: priority list was implementation-summary, spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria, decision-record, research, handover, resource-map. No goal.md!). So goal.md is a purpose carrier that no hop reads. That's a crucial finding: the lowest-cost change may be to add goal.md's Objective to the resume ladder/compaction brief — the content already exists in 94 phase parents.\n\nLet me verify:\n1. Is goal.md in SPEC_DOC_PRIORITY? No (list at 151-162). Confirm via grep for \"goal.md\" in resume-ladder.ts → expect 0.\n2. Does any hop read goal.md at all? grep across hooks/lib resume for \"goal.md\".\n\nAlso count phase parents total (for the ratio 94/N). Let me measure.\n\nThen I can rank:\n- Candidate A (parent-level acceptance criteria): 10 parents have it; template has no purpose column; would need manifest change (phase optionalAddons) + AC_CLOSURE rule scoping + create.sh seeding + template. High cost, low coverage (10 vs 94).\n- Candidate B (parent-level user story / purpose-problem section): already exists in the template — 0 new authoring benefit; doesn't cross a hop. Zero-cost no-op.\n- Candidate C (improved parent template): can add the user story to phase-parent, but no hop reads it; still fails unless a hop reads.\n- Candidate D (purpose field in continuity block): needs schema+writer+validator+parser+template; migration for 4,657 summaries.\n- Candidate E (purpose in compaction brief): needs a resolvable packet (lastSpecFolder exists) + one read + one section; ~1 file for Claude (plus dsh reuse) but no coverage on resume path.\n- Candidate F (purpose line in resume brief, sourced from spec.md `### Purpose` or goal.md Objective): 2-3 files (ladder signal + brief template row + optional facet), coverage: every resume; and goal.md exists in 94 parents, spec.md purpose in 2,943 packets.\n\nRecommendation: F (+ E if capacity) — read the already-authored purpose at the read surfaces; specifically the smallest single change is the resume brief row + ladder extraction, because resume is the canonical recovery surface every runtime delegates to (session-prime says \"Run /speckit:resume\"; dsh/pi/devin pointers all point there).\n\nCost measurement: count files touched by F: resume-ladder.ts (ResumeSignal + parser + synthesizeResult + restore panel facet), speckit-resume-presentation.txt (brief template), thin-continuity-record.ts if a facet is used. That's 2-3 files, no schema migration, no new authoring.\n\nLet me verify goal.md absence in ladder and measure parent counts. Then write iteration 4 with recommendation + cost + validation step (REQ-002 wants one recommendation with cost and validation).\n\nValidation step: after implementing, run `/speckit:resume` on a packet with a filled purpose and confirm the brief shows it; and a fixture test for the ladder (`resume-ladder.vitest.ts` exists).\n\nLet me measure."}
