face is the smallest change that closes the measured gap — add purpose to ResumeSignal, extract '### Purpose' from the spec-doc snapshot already read, and render a Purpose row in the RESUME BRIEF; two files and one test, no schema change, no migration, no new authoring.\",[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/resume/resume-ladder.ts\",\".skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-resume-presentation.txt\"]],\n [\"f-iter004-009\",\"Candidate (f) has the widest coverage per unit of effort because every runtime's recovery pointer already lands on /speckit:resume (claude session-prime, dsh, devin, pi), so one read-side addition reaches every hop the operator described.\",[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/session-prime.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/dsh/session-compact-context.mjs\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/devin/post-compaction.cjs\"]],\n [\"f-iter004-010\",\"Validation plan for the recommendation: fixture tests in resume-ladder.vitest.ts for a filled spec.md purpose, a goal.md-only carrier and a no-purpose packet, plus one manual /speckit:resume against this packet checking the rendered row.\",[\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/resume-ladder.vitest.ts\"]],\n];\nconst q4=\"Which candidate change closes the measured gap at the lowest cost? The operator's candidates, to be tested and not assumed: acceptance criteria at the parent spec level, a user story or purpose and problem section at the parent level and an improved parent-specific spec template. Add any other candidate the evidence supports, for example a purpose field in the continuity block or in the compaction brief.\";\nconst record={type:\"iteration\",iteration,runId:SID,sessionId:SID,lineageId:SID,mode:\"research\",target_agent:\"deep-research\",agent_definition_loaded:true,resolved_route:\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",run:iteration,status:\"complete\",\n focus:\"Q4 — ranking the operator's three