{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a570a9606c473d0d","status":"completed","result":"47:    reminder: \"If the runtime reports resend_pending, or the operator copy is known to be behind, render the parent goal.md chat slice once and ask the operator to set it, then continue the resume. Send the `chat_slice` that `node .skilled/hooks/goal/bin/goal.cjs packet <spec_path> --workspace <repo root>` prints. What it contains, and the `packet_budget=ok` check before it is sent, are section 4 of sk-create-goal's references/budget-and-handoff.md. On Claude Code, send it as one fenced code block that holds the slice and nothing else.\"\n75:      method: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \\\"resume work session context\\\" (exit 0 = hits, 1 = clean no-hit, 2+ = error; a no-hit falls through, never guesses)\"\n78:      method: \"glob {.opencode/,}specs/**/{handover.md,implementation-summary.md,tasks.md} | filter active folders | sort by mtime | head -1\"\n86:  fallback: { on_no_memory: \"Report no active session, suggest /speckit:complete\" }\n92:  order: [\"Primary: handover.md (<24h old)\", \"Primary: _memory.continuity in implementation-summary.md\", \"Primary: supporting spec docs (tasks/plan/decision-record/resource-map)\", \"Secondary: graph-metadata.json packet hints\", \"Secondary: the packet-scoped ripgrep context recipe (retrieval-conventions.md section 2.4) for a named gap\"]\n93:  note: \"Recover from the canonical packet first: handover, then _memory.continuity, then supporting spec docs. The ripgrep recipe fills a named gap only. Nothing here needs a background service.\"\n98:  constraint: \"Never replace the canonical handover/continuity/spec-doc recovery ladder.\"\n102:  behavior: \"Auto-load handover.md (<24h) first, else walk the continuity ladder without prompting; stop as soon as one safe next action can be named\"\n105:  continuity_ladder:\n108:      - \"Read {spec_folder_path}/handover.md when present and recent\"\n109:      - \"Read the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder_path}/implementation-summary.md\"\n114:smart_memory_logic:\n119:    - \"If current phase or task is missing, inspect tasks.md/acceptance-criteria.md/handover.md\"\n120:    - \"If next safe action is missing, read `_memory.continuity`, then run the packet-scoped ripgrep context recipe on next-steps/state anchors\"\n138:  reply_format: [\"Confidence: NN%\", \"Context source: handover|memory\", \"Now\", \"Last confirmed\", \"Next safe action\"]\n155:    outputs: { spec_folder: detected_path, detection_method: argument_or_memory }\n158:  step_2_load_memory:\n159:    purpose: Load context using handover first, then recover only the missing essentials needed for a useful resume\n161:      - Check for handover.md in spec_folder (<24h old)\n162:      - If recent handover exists, load as primary context\n163:      - If handover is absent or insufficient, read `_memory.continuity` from implementation-summary.md\n169:    context_priority: [\"handover.md\", \"_memory.continuity\", \"supporting spec docs\", \"packet-scoped ripgrep context recipe\", \"packet-scoped ripgrep anchor recipe\"]\n174:    outputs: { memory_loaded: true, context_source: \"handover|continuity|spec_docs|ripgrep_context|ripgrep_anchor\", context_summary: extracted_context, resume_packet: \"now|last|next|blockers|artifact\" }\n207:  description: \"Recovery is handled inside the resume workflow through handover.md, then _memory.continuity, then supporting spec docs, with a packet-scoped ripgrep recipe only when the canonical packet is thin\"\n208:  when_to_use: [\"Session interrupted unexpectedly\", \"Context compaction detected\", \"Need to recover without handover.md\"]\n"}
